---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Send one JSON-RPC call (an endpoint with a method, or a request file) and print its result or error object

Usage: rustman rpc call [OPTIONS] <ENDPOINT|REQUEST> [METHOD] [PARAMS_JSON]

Arguments:
  <ENDPOINT|REQUEST>
          An endpoint URL (http, https, ws, wss, or a {{variable}}), or a jsonrpc request file, its id or its name

  [METHOD]
          The method to call (with an endpoint)

  [PARAMS_JSON]
          The params, as a JSON array or object

Options:
  -H, --header <NAME: VALUE>
          Add a header (repeatable): --header "Authorization: Basic {{auth}}"

      --id <ID>
          Send this id instead of 1 (an integer, or else a string)

      --notify
          Send a notification: no id, no response expected

      --subscribe <NOTIFICATION>
          Subscribe: METHOD is the subscribe method and this the notification method (needs --unsubscribe and a ws:// or wss:// endpoint)

      --unsubscribe <METHOD>
          The method that ends a subscription

      --max-events <N>
          Subscriptions stop after N events (default: the request's max_events, else 10)

      --duration <DURATION>
          Subscriptions stop after this long (default: the request's max_duration_ms, else 30s)

      --no-validate
          Send even when the call does not match the endpoint's OpenRPC catalog

      --raw
          Print the response envelopes as received (redacted)

      --json
          Print the whole exchange as one JSON object

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or a number of milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates (exchanges are flagged insecure)

      --no-history
          Do not record the exchanges in history

      --trace
          Send trace context (traceparent) even when no trace block enables it

  -u, --update-snapshots
          Overwrite snapshots that differ from the response (not in CI mode)

      --ci
          CI mode: never write snapshots, and fail on a missing one (also on when the CI variable is true or 1)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
